-- title:
--   Kernel degree from a presenting ideal with constant fibre rank
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative ring, $u : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ a pair of two-variable formal power series over $B$ (an element of `Series B`), $I$ an ideal of $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$, and $h$ a natural number. Assume that the ideal generated by the two components of $u$ equals $I$; that the quotient $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/I$ is a finite $B$-module; that it is a projective $B$-module; and that for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/I^{f}$ has finite dimension $p^{h}$, where $I^{f}$ denotes the image of $I$ under the coefficientwise map $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!] \to \kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ induced by $f$. The conclusion is `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree u (p ^ h)`, i.e. that the three clauses of that predicate hold for $u$ with degree $p^{h}$: the kernel algebra $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/(u_0,u_1)$ is a finite $B$-module, it is a projective $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$ one has $\dim_{\kappa} \kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/(f(u_0), f(u_1)) = p^{h}$, the components of $u$ being mapped coefficientwise.
--
--   This is the bookkeeping step that converts a presentation of a finite locally free subgroup scheme by an ideal $I$ with prescribed fibre ranks into the kernel-degree clause used in the definition of an isogeny of height $h$ of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules. It is invoked in the construction of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module structures on quotients by finite locally free subgroups, for instance in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates).
